INT. ESCAPE ROOM - "THE MUMMY'S CRYPT" - DAY

A fake tomb: painted hieroglyphs, a plastic sarcophagus, torches with flickering LED flames. A timer on the wall counts down: 04:12. A speaker hisses behind the sphinx, and nobody pays it any attention.

Five coworkers in matching "TEAMWORK!" T-shirts mill around a stone table. BRENDA KOWALSKI (50s, regional manager, laminated agenda) reads the instructions aloud to no one. KAREEM ALLEN (30s, analyst, hands in pockets) stares at the walls. FENELLA OKAFOR-LISTER (40s, accountant, wire-rim glasses) has already found three clues and hidden them in her pocket. OLUWASEUN ADEYEMI (20s, new hire, smiling too hard) rattles a locked chest. TRIXIE VANCE (30s, sales, huge hoop earrings) leans on the sarcophagus, scrolling her phone.

BRENDA
Okay, team, okay. Let's circle up. Circle up!

Nobody circles. Brenda circles herself. The timer reads 03:58.

KAREEM
Brenda, there's a chest.

BRENDA
Great. Oluwaseun, open the chest.

OLUWASEUN
It's locked.

BRENDA
Then unlock it.

OLUWASEUN
With what?

BRENDA
With teamwork!

Fenella steps to the table, takes a scrap of papyrus from her pocket, and lays it flat. Kareem leans over it, and Trixie pockets her phone and drifts over, and Oluwaseun abandons the chest. All four heads converge, and Brenda, in the way of the circle, is somehow left outside it.

FENELLA
It's a cipher. The sun disc means three.

KAREEM
What's the jackal?

FENELLA
Seven.

TRIXIE
Where'd you get the paper?

FENELLA
Under the sarcophagus.

TRIXIE
You didn't tell us.

FENELLA
Nobody asked.

BRENDA
Fenella, we agreed no hoarding.

FENELLA
We agreed on a synergy workshop. I'm hoarding.

KAREEM
Three, seven--

OLUWASEUN
Is there an eye? There's an eye on the chest.

TRIXIE
Eye equals one.

KAREEM
Three seven one!

Oluwaseun spins the dials. The chest clicks open. Inside, a plastic scarab and a note.

OLUWASEUN
It says, "The real treasure was the friends we made."

BRENDA
(moved)
That's lovely.

FENELLA
That's the worst clue I've ever read.

TRIXIE
Where's the door?

The timer reads 00:41.

KAREEM
Brenda! Brenda, which wall?

BRENDA
I don't know! I made an agenda, I didn't make a map!

Oluwaseun begins to hum. Fenella looks at the ceiling. Trixie heaves the sarcophagus lid aside to reveal a door handle in the back, and the five of them stampede toward it, crash into each other, and tumble together in a heap on the cold fake stone.

The timer hits zero. The torches go out.

BRENDA (CONT'D)
(in the dark)
I think that went well.
